critic.text:
Stale/unsupported: the WaPo/Schar poll is older than one week; the D+8–9 generic-ballot claim lacks a dated source; no actual Election Day results exist. Double counting: all panelists lean on the same DCCC internal and the same toss-up ratings, so they are not independent signals. Ignored base rates: VA-01 backed Trump by ~5 and Wittman won 2024 by 12.9 points; incumbency and GOP lean argue for a Democratic probability near 50%, not 78%.

Panel disagreement: Claude gives a slight Dem edge (0.52), while GPT/Gemini keep Wittman favored (0.47–0.48). GPT/Gemini are more convincing: district partisanship and incumbency outweigh one partisan internal poll and a national-mood assumption. The market’s 0.78 is not justified by the cited toss-up polls/ratings unless it has unreported early-vote or turnout information; it looks overpriced.

