panel.text:
I put the probability of a Democratic House majority at **94%**. The base rate favors the party out of the White House in a midterm, and Republicans’ narrow current majority leaves little room for losses. The roughly D+9 generic-ballot lead and district ratings pointing toward Democratic gains reinforce that advantage.

It is not certain: Democrats defend several Trump-won districts, Florida’s new map creates additional risks for them, and polling error or uneven turnout could narrow the expected gains. The brief offers limited evidence that candidate quality or Election Day developments have materially changed the national picture. No results are available yet.

{"p_dem":0.94,"key_reasons":"Out-party midterm advantage, narrow Republican majority, roughly D+9 polling lead, and district ratings favor Democrats; polling error and district-level risks prevent certainty."}

