* **Ratings, Candidate Quality & Late News:** Major non-partisan handicappers show overwhelming consensus for a sizable Democratic wave. On October 30, 2026, *Cook Political Report* projected a Democratic net gain of 12 to 22 (or up to 25) seats and placed 218–220 seats as favored for Democrats outright. On November 2, 2026, *Inside Elections* projected a Democratic pickup of 20 to 30 seats, and *Sabato's Crystal Ball* rated more than 218 seats as "Leans Democratic" or safer without needing any toss-ups. Across major raters, 291 individual rating shifts moved in Democrats' favor between Labor Day and October 30, 2026, pushing even deep-red seats like FL-22 (Trump +14) and MT-01 (Trump +11.5) into competitive territory. While a slight tail risk of an unprecedented polling miss remains, the fundamentals and district-level indicators point overwhelmingly toward a Democratic House majority.

